Jinja's own test cases, extracted.

Source:  https://github.com/pallets/jinja
Commit:  5ef70112a1ff19c05324ff889dd30405b1002044
Fetched: 2026-08-21

cases.json holds the triples that could be lifted out of Jinja's
pytest suite without interpreting Python: a template built from a
string literal by env.from_string, rendered with literal keyword
arguments, and compared with == against a string literal. Anything
using a fixture, a custom filter, an expected exception, or async is
left behind, which is why 238 cases come out of 8000 lines of tests.

SPEC section 31 asks for "the Jinja project's own test cases where
they apply to the supported subset". Where they do not apply, the
case still runs and its disagreement is recorded with the reason, in
internal/template/corpus_test.go.

Regenerate with tools/vendor-jinja-corpus.sh.

